<title>USA: Equidex says arbitrator rules against Dow.</title>
<headline>Equidex says arbitrator rules against Dow.</headline>
<dateline>GUTTENBERG, N.J. 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Equidex said an arbitrator awarded its commodities publishing unit, Commodex, a $4.15 million award against Dow Jones &amp; Co Inc's Telerate unit over a contract dispute.</p>
<p>Equidex said the claim arose from a contract that allowed Telerate to distribute Commodex's information, which provides &quot;buy&quot; and &quot;sell&quot; signals for futures markets, over the Telerate network on a revenue sharing basis.</p>
<p>Dow Jones representatives were not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
